# frontend
# --------
# IMPORTANT: this is NOT a normal Vite build-time env var (no VITE_ prefix,
# not read by import.meta.env). It's read by YOUR container's entrypoint
# SHELL SCRIPT at container startup, which does something like:
#
#   envsubst '${GREETING_SERVICE_URL}' < /usr/share/nginx/html/config.template.js \
#     > /usr/share/nginx/html/config.js
#
# That produces config.js, which sets window.__APP_CONFIG__.GREETING_SERVICE_URL
# — read by src/App.jsx at page load, in the browser. So this env var lives
# on the POD (set via ConfigMap/Deployment), not baked into the JS bundle
# at `docker build` time. That's what makes one image portable across
# environments without a rebuild.
#
# Local dev (npm run dev) doesn't use this at all — it reads
# public/config.js directly, which already defaults to "/api".

# What the BROWSER needs to be able to reach — i.e. an externally-facing
# URL/path, not an internal ClusterIP DNS name (the browser is outside
# the cluster and can't resolve *.svc.cluster.local).

# If your Ingress routes a path prefix like /api/* to greeting-service:
GREETING_SERVICE_URL=/api

# If you're exposing greeting-service directly via NodePort instead of
# Ingress, use the full reachable URL, e.g.:
# GREETING_SERVICE_URL=http://<minikube-ip>:<node-port>
